  "note": "Election of the whole council (21 members, seven for each of the North, South and West wards) on 15 January 1932. Only the West Ward was contested; North and South were filled unopposed (Irish News, 6 January 1932, p. 8; Belfast News-Letter, 16 January 1932, p. 7). The retiring members were Messrs. Nugent, Starrs and M'Conville. Citation unconfirmed: the names were not all found on the cited page (verification 5 Nov 2026)."
